@node Top
@top Tweeta Desktop

@insertcopying

Tweeta Desktop is a GTK3 desktop client for the Tweeta/Tweetapus social
platform.

@menu
* Overview::
* Invoking tweeta-desktop::
* Environment Variables::
* Files::
* Feature Summary::
* License::
@end menu

@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Tweeta Desktop provides a native desktop interface for timelines, profiles,
search, notifications, direct messages, and moderation/admin features.

Current runtime support is Linux.

@node Invoking tweeta-desktop
@chapter Invoking tweeta-desktop

Run the program as:

@example
tweeta-desktop
@end example

Tweeta Desktop does not define custom command-line options. Standard GTK3
options are supported.

@node Environment Variables
@chapter Environment Variables

@table @code
@item TWEETA_API_BASE_URL
Overrides the default API base URL used for API requests.

@item TWEETA_BASE_DOMAIN
Overrides the default site base domain used for absolute web/media URLs.

@item XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory used by GLib for per-user configuration.

@item XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory used by GLib for per-user cache data.
@end table

@node Files
@chapter Files

@table @file
@item $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tweeta-desktop/session.json
Stores session token, username, and admin flag after a successful login.

@item $XDG_CACHE_HOME/tweeta-desktop/
Cache directory used by cache management in the Settings view.
@end table

@node Feature Summary
@chapter Feature Summary

@itemize @bullet
@item Public and following timelines with infinite scroll.
@item User authentication (login/logout) with session restore.
@item Composing posts with optional media uploads.
@item Reply, like, retweet/quote, bookmark, and emoji reaction actions.
@item Search for users and posts.
@item Profile views with tweets/replies/followers/following.
@item Notifications inbox and mark-all-read action.
@item Direct messages, including encrypted messaging with GPG keys.
@item Communities browsing and join/leave actions.
@item Admin views for site stats, users, posts, and moderation actions.
@item Settings for theme, compact mode, notifications, and cache cleanup.
@end itemize

